YASD, those first 15 minutes are the most dangerous!

Coming back to a promising caveman after a very late session
the night before, I couldn't figure out exactly what I was
doing when I quit. I was 3 levels below minetown, my pack
was full, I was burdened and my pet was missing! Must have
been playing in my sleep there toward the end.

So I decided to make my way back to Minetown and do some
sorting and stashing. The mines weren't very challenging to
a XL9 dwarf with a -4 AC. I soon discovered how I came to my
current situation, the next level up was partially mapped
and only the downstairs had been discovered, so I mapped the
rest of this level and was on my way to the stairs when I
stumbled across a land mine, injuring my legs and becoming
stressed!

I figured they would heal before I got to the stairs but I
was wrong. Even so, nothing in the mines had come even
remotely close to killing me yet, that is until the
leocrotta showed up. First attack, 25/64. Now you'd think an
experienced player with a /oDeath, /oDigging and
/oTeleportation would escape from this situation without any
serious thought. Trouble is, I gave it no thought and one
more step, DYWYPI?

I guess I just hadn't quite gotten focused on the game
again! Sigh!
